{"title":"Sharma Math Exam 2026 Problems/Problem 1","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Sharma_Math_Exam_2026_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A gardener stands in a triangular courtyard \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> with side lengths <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/a/1faf03033f1dba03fb05985e5ef5eb60dcdff425.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$13, 14$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"44\" height=\"16\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/9/f1965fae079a9ba2c0726c307070c2355dfcb213.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> meters. He places a pivot point on the southern boundary line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> which has length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/0/820a20de2847dfdc1bc5cffc8d904933150032bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$14$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> meters and spins a long, horizontal pruning stick around it, which clears a circular path <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/d/54d7d48553f4d9e7ab418118607ea324cbfddfda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" />. If the stick is exactly long enough to just graze the two adjacent walls <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a179ff2638e4799cadd820db205c2beff6299ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> as it spins, what is the radius of the area swept by the stick in meters?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/9/d7933d9ddb1dc62b0256735f36927fa43ccaefb2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) } \\frac{8}{3} \\qquad\\textbf{(B) } \\frac{10}{3} \\qquad\\textbf{(C) } 4 \\qquad\\textbf{(D) } \\frac{17}{4} \\qquad\\textbf{(E) } 6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"385\" height=\"38\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Diagram\">Diagram</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Sharma_Math_Exam_2026_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Diagram\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Note: it doesn't matter whether <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> is on the left or right. WLOG here we put it on the left.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/1/42123950c1736ec9f31ecdb366bd18098b9e97f6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] size(250);  pair B = (0,0); pair C = (14,0); pair A = (5,12);  draw(A--B--C--cycle);  // center on BC determined from equal distance to AB and AC pair O = (84/13,0); label(&quot;$O$&quot;, O, SW);  // tangency points pair T1 = foot(O,A,B); pair T2 = foot(O,A,C);  real r = length(O-T1);  draw(circle(O,r)); draw(O--T1); draw(O--T2);  // radius labels label(&quot;$r$&quot;, midpoint(O--T1), NE); label(&quot;$r$&quot;, midpoint(O--T2), NW);  // connect A to circle center draw(A--O, dashed);  label(&quot;$A$&quot;, A, N); label(&quot;$B$&quot;, B, SW); label(&quot;$C$&quot;, C, SE); label(&quot;$\\omega$&quot;, O, N);  label(&quot;$13$&quot;, midpoint(A--B), NW); label(&quot;$14$&quot;, midpoint(B--C), S); label(&quot;$15$&quot;, midpoint(A--C), NE);  dot(A); dot(B); dot(C); dot(O); [/asy]\" width=\"355\" height=\"418\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Sharma_Math_Exam_2026_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The area of the triangle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/6/fb6282faf6a7c0646bd49eca45b23e752ebad101.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{21\\cdot 8 \\cdot 7 \\cdot 6} = 84$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"144\" height=\"21\" /> by Heron's Formula. This makes the length of the altitude from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/f/edf074831eb5bc9e61d6d6e09f525a86e3068f6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. By the Angle Bisector Theorem, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/3/0a35417b9cceeb039441b86390f1b0fe44d164a7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BO = \\frac{13}{2}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"82\" height=\"38\" /> \n</p><p>Letting point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> be the origin, the coordinates of point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/5/d657e158d8ed47cc07263f93051a456ba88df9fb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(5, 12)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"47\" height=\"18\" /> and the coordinates of point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/d/1adfe99f2690201f4b9ec3888220b4afe4c5bd8d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(\\frac{13}{2}, 0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"55\" height=\"38\" />. The equation of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/0/3c056ac24c4a9a15d938726451a8b766162e9a4c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12x - 5y = 0.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"110\" height=\"17\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is the distance between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/4/d3431b737f3671c3c1d717f039984ff101e97404.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"32\" height=\"16\" /> which is \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/3/e1372de767da59089ba03b879cfd043e839972ec.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{12\\cdot \\frac{13}{2} - 5\\cdot 0}{\\sqrt{12^2 + 5^2}} = \\boxed{\\textbf{(E) } 6}.\\]\" width=\"186\" height=\"45\" />\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018041100\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.017 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.052 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 111/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 5718/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    0.000      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:36056:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018041100 and revision id 281989. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}